{"login": "sharm999", "location": "Michigan, USA", "commits": [{"sha": "cb9005e3f399ae880bc89140dac0ca2c82c4df2a", "message": "Created using Colab", "created_at": "2025-03-04T20:36:55Z", "repo": "python_codes_cgan", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "eebe780e205ebddc628962f0d2c15ebe507efc88", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2023-02-01T21:43:40Z", "repo": "python_codes_cgan", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "4263c97e40c63c10a8222877650d19b110b2f932", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2023-02-01T21:43:04Z", "repo": "python_codes_cgan", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "0a2ab2e7659fcc6913740547cd06bfd4871e83c4", "message": "Initial commit", "created_at": "2023-02-01T21:41:53Z", "repo": "python_codes_cgan", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "c597fdd13bf9c8c8036a2852a26ec4409f55f996", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2026-01-22T20:07:11Z", "repo": "Geosptial_Maps_by_R", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "e6af8896e6c9aae9defa2d5bbe31636e77f54eb2", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2026-01-22T20:03:42Z", "repo": "Geosptial_Maps_by_R", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "2ddcb022bc1f5bf1223998c427076164cd2fcfad", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2026-01-22T20:02:10Z", "repo": "Geosptial_Maps_by_R", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "d70b121019601e2f595b2fc993e3ef5256dced42", "message": "Delete India_Bivariate_Climate_CHELSA_bio1_bio12.png", "created_at": "2026-01-22T20:01:36Z", "repo": "Geosptial_Maps_by_R", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "8b9aa06ccafddc57e78504c0898f7a91119b26c5", "message": "Add files via upload\n\nWhat it shows: Each pixel encodes two variables at once from CHELSA Bioclim\u2014bio1 (mean annual temperature) on the x-axis of the legend (\u2192 warmer to the right) and bio12 (annual precipitation) on the y-axis (\u2191 wetter upward). Colors are a 3\u00d73 bivariate scheme, so similar colors mean similar temp\u2013rainfall combinations.\r\n\r\nPatterns visible:\r\nWestern India (Rajasthan, parts of Gujarat): predominantly hot\u2013dry shades.\r\nIndo-Gangetic Plain (Punjab \u2192 Bihar): warm with increasing moisture eastward - colors shift upward across the legend.\r\nWestern Ghats & Konkan coast (Kerala, coastal Karnataka/Maharashtra): hot\u2013wet ribbon along the windward slopes.\r\nDeccan interior (rain-shadow): warm\u2013dry to moderately wet, reflecting the drop in monsoon rainfall inland.\r\nNortheast (Assam, Meghalaya, Nagaland, etc.): very wet, mostly warm\u2013wet to cool\u2013wet at higher elevations.\r\nHimalayan belt: transitions from cool\u2013wet (middle slopes) to cool\u2013dry in the high, cold rain-shadow (Ladakh/Trans-Himalaya).\r\nTamil Nadu\u2019s southeast coast: relatively warm\u2013drier compared to the west coast.\r\nAndaman & Nicobar: warm\u2013wet maritime regime.\r\n\r\nWhy it\u2019s useful: The bivariate palette makes joint gradients obvious for e.g., monsoon-driven west-to-east wetting across the plains, and topographic effects (wet windward vs. dry leeward slopes). It\u2019s a compact climate backdrop for comparing crop zones, heat/humidity risk, or selecting sites for field studies.", "created_at": "2026-01-22T20:00:59Z", "repo": "Geosptial_Maps_by_R", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "dc780bee4621741e8bc6e52273e83c257079300d", "message": "Delete India_Bivariate_Climate_CHELSA_bio1_bio12.png", "created_at": "2026-01-22T19:53:22Z", "repo": "Geosptial_Maps_by_R", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "19f82fc642428bc2e7da21908275dc26179daea5", "message": "Add files via upload\n\nBivariate Map for India Country by using the CHELSA BioClimate. Temperature and Percipitation used.", "created_at": "2026-01-22T19:46:50Z", "repo": "Geosptial_Maps_by_R", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ac31c284e644dfe24705f0ab243dcd06de4281c4", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2026-01-12T17:30:12Z", "repo": "Geosptial_Maps_by_R", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "d403c5897555d99c53d05be5c16297a7f191d29a", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2026-01-12T17:29:52Z", "repo": "Geosptial_Maps_by_R", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "3aaba7009a3f78418867c4796dd96130034f3200", "message": "Update Bivariate_Map_Midwest.r", "created_at": "2026-01-12T17:28:57Z", "repo": "Geosptial_Maps_by_R", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "700a0200034b9bdbde086bd507567f8a85220db4", "message": "Update Bivariate_Map_Midwest.r", "created_at": "2026-01-12T17:28:13Z", "repo": "Geosptial_Maps_by_R", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "648c32923a569a854488d228c8cc4c0e03984955", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2026-01-12T17:26:52Z", "repo": "Geosptial_Maps_by_R", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "fd8c74f823f4011ffb4246c28d15a929c7b668a4", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2026-01-12T17:26:17Z", "repo": "Geosptial_Maps_by_R", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "178d358d8eb8188a25dc8bc08bc0e78c09954e09", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2026-01-12T17:25:11Z", "repo": "Geosptial_Maps_by_R", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "082bddfb1456a4533b97b018ca693cff9e3b2936", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2026-01-12T17:24:50Z", "repo": "Geosptial_Maps_by_R", "file_sampled": fals